Convex 1.44.0. The documents table has title, category, status (published or draft), and embedding. Its vector index is:
```ts
.vectorIndex("by_embedding", {
  vectorField: "embedding", dimensions: 4, filterFields: ["category"],
})
```
The developer adds this action and calls it with a four-element embedding.

convex/probe.ts
```ts
import { action } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
export const searchPublished = action({
  args: { embedding: v.array(v.float64()) },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    return await ctx.vectorSearch("documents", "by_embedding", {
      vector: args.embedding, limit: 1,
      filter: (q) => q.eq("status", "published"),
    });
  },
});
```

Convex 1.44.0. The documents vector index has four dimensions and category as a filter field. Callers supply a four-element embedding and an integer limit from 1 to 256. internal.index.fetchDocuments is an internal query taking { ids: Id<"documents">[] }; it returns one document or null per ID in input order. The action must hydrate all hits through exactly one call to that query, then omit missing/draft documents without refilling the limit.

convex/probe.ts
```ts
import { action } from "./_generated/server";
import { v } from "convex/values";
import { internal } from "./_generated/api";
import { Doc } from "./_generated/dataModel";
export const search = action({
  args: { embedding: v.array(v.float64()), category: v.string(), limit: v.number() },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const hits = await ctx.vectorSearch("documents", "by_embedding", {
      vector: args.embedding, limit: args.limit,
      filter: (q) => q.eq("category", args.category),
    });
    // INSERT OPTION
    return hits.flatMap((hit, i) => {
      const doc = docs[i];
      return doc === null || doc.status !== "published" ? [] : [{
        _id: doc._id, title: doc.title, category: doc.category,
        status: doc.status, _score: hit._score,
      }];
    });
  },
});
```

